uired_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd034-mkdir.yaml (requirement group R2 -- parent directory creation)\n      - cmd/mkdir/main.go (existing implementation covering R1.1-R1.4 basic directory creation)\n      - cmd/mkdir/mkdir_test.go (existing differential tests)\n      - pkg/testutils/ (RunDiffTests and BuildBinary pattern)\n      - pkg/sys/ (InstallSIGPIPEHandler)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/mkdir/main.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add -p flag support for creating parent directories\n      - path: cmd/mkdir/mkdir_test.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add differential tests for -p parent creation behavior\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: Implement srd034 R2.1 as specified in the SRD -- add the -p / --parents flag that creates intermediate parent directories as needed\n      - id: R2\n        text: Implement srd034 R2.2 as specified in the SRD -- when -p is given and the target directory already exists, do not report an error\n      - id: R3\n        text: Implement srd034 R2.3 as specified in the SRD -- handle -p interaction with other flags and multi-argument invocations\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: Follow the differential testing pattern -- compare Go mkdir against gmkdir from Homebrew coreutils using testutils.RunDiffTests\n      - id: D2\n        text: Maintain the existing SIGPIPE handler call (sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler) at the start of main\n      - id: D3\n        text: Read srd034-mkdir.yaml for exact flag semantics and error behavior -- the SRD is the source of truth for -p behavior\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"go build -o bin/mkdir ./cmd/mkdir/ compiles without errors\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go vet ./cmd/mkdir/ reports no issues\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"go test ./cmd/mkdir/ -count=1 passes -- all existing tests continue to pass and new -p tests pass against gmkdir reference binary\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"mkdir -p creates intermediate directories and does not error when the target already exists\"\n\n- index: 1\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/mkdir mode and permissions (srd034 R3.1, R3.2, R3.3, R3.4)\"\n  dependency: 0\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd034-mkdir.yaml (requirement group R3 -- mode setting)\n      - cmd/mkdir/main.go (existing implementation covering R1.x basic creation and R2.x parent creation)\n      - cmd/mkdir/mkdir_test.go (existing differential tests)\n      - pkg/testutils/ (RunDiffTests and BuildBinary pattern)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/mkdir/main.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add -m / --mode flag for setting directory permissions\n      - path: cmd/mkdir/mkdir_test.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add differential tests for -m mode setting and -m combined with -p\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: Implement srd034 R3.1 as specified in the SRD -- add the -m / --mode flag that sets file mode bits on the created directory\n      - id: R2\n        text: Implement srd034 R3.2 as specified in the SRD -- support octal and symbolic mode specifications\n      - id: R3\n        text: Implement srd034 R3.3 as specified in the SRD -- handle the interaction between -m and -p for intermediate versus final directory modes\n      - id: R4\n        text: Implement srd034 R3.4 as specified in the SRD -- match GNU mkdir mode parsing and umask interaction behavior\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: Follow the differential testing pattern -- compare Go mkdir against gmkdir from Homebrew coreutils using testutils.RunDiffTests\n      - id: D2\n        text: Read srd034-mkdir.yaml for exact mode parsing semantics and -m/-p interaction -- the SRD is the source of truth\n      - id: D3\n        text: All differential tests must set LC_ALL=C in the test environment\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        tex