fTests\n      - id: D2\n        text: Read srd034-mkdir.yaml for exact error message formats and exit code values -- the SRD is the source of truth\n      - id: D3\n        text: Error messages must go to stderr; exit code 1 for errors, 0 for success, matching GNU behavior\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"go build -o bin/mkdir ./cmd/mkdir/ compiles without errors\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go vet ./cmd/mkdir/ reports no issues\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"go test ./cmd/mkdir/ -count=1 passes -- all tests pass against gmkdir reference binary\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"mkdir on a path with permission denied writes an error to stderr and exits with code 1\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"mkdir --version and mkdir --help produce output and exit 0\"\n\n- index: 3\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/rmdir basic directory removal (srd035 R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R1.4)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd035-rmdir.yaml (requirement group R1 -- basic directory removal)\n      - cmd/mkdir/main.go (reference for directory utility structure and flag parsing pattern)\n      - pkg/testutils/ (RunDiffTests, BuildBinary, DiffTest pattern)\n      - pkg/sys/ (InstallSIGPIPEHandler)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/rmdir/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: rmdir implementation -- basic empty directory removal with argument handling\n      - path: cmd/rmdir/rmdir_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Differential tests comparing Go rmdir against grmdir reference binary\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: Implement srd035 R1.1 as specified in the SRD -- remove each directory argument that is empty, reporting an error for non-empty directories\n      - id: R2\n        text: Implement srd035 R1.2 as specified in the SRD -- support multiple directory arguments, processing each in order and continuing after errors\n      - id: R3\n        text: Implement srd035 R1.3 as specified in the SRD -- match GNU rmdir error messages and exit codes (exit 0 on all success, exit 1 if any removal fails)\n      - id: R4\n        text: Implement srd035 R1.4 as specified in the SRD -- handle edge cases such as non-existent directories, paths that are files, and permission denied\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: Call sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at the start of main to match GNU coreutils SIGPIPE behavior\n      - id: D2\n        text: Use the differential testing pattern -- BuildBinary for Go binary, exec.LookPath for grmdir reference, t.Skip if reference not found\n      - id: D3\n        text: Set LC_ALL=C in all differential test environments\n      - id: D4\n        text: Read srd035-rmdir.yaml for exact error message format and flag semantics -- the SRD is the source of truth\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"go build -o bin/rmdir ./cmd/rmdir/ compiles without errors\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go vet ./cmd/rmdir/ reports no issues\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"go test ./cmd/rmdir/ -count=1 passes -- differential tests pass against grmdir reference binary\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"rmdir removes an empty directory and exits 0\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"rmdir on a non-empty directory writes an error to stderr and exits 1\"\n      - id: AC6\n        text: \"rmdir with multiple arguments processes all arguments, continuing after errors\"\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"0a1de9f8-f4df-4f6e-bd59-b8abe94cc19f","total_cost_usd":0.70215275,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":53665,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"output_tokens":12697,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":53665,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":12697,"cache_re